maya: customer report — streaming stops ~30s in Vercel Edge after auth token rotation. they see a 401 then the ReadableStream never emits end, app shows a stalled UI. using @redwood/sdk-js in an edge function (next/edge). repro below.

maya: repro (minimal edge handler):
```js
export default async function handler(req) {
  const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
  const res = await client.responses.stream({ model: 'o16v-chat', input: 'hello' });
  // in edge runtime we pipe the readable to response
  return new Response(res.body, { headers: { 'Content-Type': 'text/event-stream' } });
}
```

maya: logs show: `HTTP 401` at token rotate time, then `ReadableStream` stops yielding; console: `TypeError: stream.cancel is not a function` in edge environment. customer on sdk-js@1.4.0.

sam: can you paste package.json / bundler target? are you setting `edge` in next config?

maya: package.json: "@redwood/sdk-js": "1.4.0", "next": "13.5.4". yes `export const runtime = 'edge'` in the api route.

alex: quick hypothesis: older SDK used a Node ReadableStream polyfill that doesn't map cleanly to V8's Web ReadableStream when bundled. token rotation causing 401 mid-stream then SDK calls `.cancel()` on the stream which isn't present in that polyfill -> hang.

alex: try two experiments: 1) upgrade to @redwood/sdk-js@1.5.2 (we fixed a stream-signal/edge mismatch) 2) add a short abort timeout around the fetch so rotated token triggers clean close.

maya: tried 1.5.2 quickly — behavior improved but still occasional stalls on long streams (>45s). i can share full logs.

