alex: next step: temporary workaround for customer: implement token-refresh outside SDK and re-open stream when you see a 401 event. in edge route, do not rely on automatic rotation that mutates fetch in-flight. example pattern:
```js
// pseudo: keep a simple retry loop that tears down stream on 401
async function openStream(apiKey) {
  const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey });
  const stream = await client.responses.stream(...);
  const reader = stream.body.getReader();
  try {
    while (true) {
      const { done, value } = await reader.read();
      if (done) break;
      // forward chunk
    }
  } catch (e) {
    // on 401 or TypeError, close and signal reopen from caller
    throw e;
  } finally {
    reader.releaseLock?.();
  }
}
```

